# GraphiQ agent rules

Follow [docs/GRAPHIQ_BUILD_GUIDE.md](docs/GRAPHIQ_BUILD_GUIDE.md). Implement only the next incomplete checklist step. Do not skip steps. Do not invent diagram kinds or replace the locked stack.

## Models

- Plan: Grok 4.6 Extra High
- Build: Composer 2.5
- If the step is marked **Escalate**, stop and tell the user to run it with Grok 4.6 Extra High (raise thinking if it still fails). Do not implement Escalate steps on Composer 2.5.

## Local `dev` only

- Build and verify on this machine. Deploy is not verification.
- Work only on `dev`. If you are not on `dev`, check it out before editing.
- After a step is done, commit on `dev`, then push `dev` to `origin` (`git push -u origin dev`). Never force-push.

## Self-review before commit

Re-read the full diff. Stay inside the step’s allowed paths. Fix every issue (types, rules, notation, tests, exhaustive `switch`/`never`). Re-run the step’s verification. Then commit and push. Do not commit a known broken step.

## Git identity (every commit)

Never run `git config`. Never use Cursor Agent as author or committer. Never `--no-verify` unless the user asks. Never `Co-authored-by`.

```bash
git -c user.name="Senuka Deneth" -c user.email="113520257+Senuka-Deneth@users.noreply.github.com" commit -m "$(cat <<'EOF'
Add <what this step added>

EOF
)"
git push -u origin dev
```

Message: one imperative sentence of what was added. No author line. No “documentation updated” / “docs updated”. GitHub contributors must remain only Senuka Deneth. Never force-push.
